    "sourceUrl": "https://www.h3c.com/en/Support/Resource_Center/EN/Switches/Catalog/S5130S/S5130S-EI/Technical_Documents/Product_Literature/Hardware_Information___Specifications/H3C_S5130S-EI_IG/202306/1867335_294551_0.htm",
    "note": "370 W total PoE power, 30 W maximum a port, on the 24 gigabit copper ports only - the two 10GBASE-T ports are the multigig pair and are not PSE ports. Vendor PoE table: 24 ports at 15.4 W (802.3af) or 12 at 30 W (802.3at)."
  },
  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 128000,
    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "Port switching capacity 128 Gbps (24 x 1G + 2 x 10G copper + 2 x 10G SFP+, full duplex), forwarding capacity 96 Mpps."
  },
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.h3c.com/en/Products_and_Solutions/InterConnect/Switches/Products/Campus_Network/Access/S5130/H3C_S5130S_EI/",
  "notes": "S5130S-EI common platform (Comware 7): box switching capacity 336 Gbps, 256 MB flash / 512 MB SDRAM, IRF2 stacking of up to 9 units, static routes plus RIP and OSPF, 802.1Q VLAN, LACP, STP/RSTP/MSTP, DHCP server, SNMPv1/v2c/v3, NETCONF/gRPC, web UI and CLI. Port layout and PoE totals from the vendor hardware-information page (https://www.h3c.com/en/Support/Resource_Center/EN/Switches/Catalog/S5130S/S5130S-EI/Technical_Documents/Product_Literature/Hardware_Information___Specifications/H3C_S5130S-EI_IG/202306/1867335_294551_0.htm); switching and forwarding figures from the vendor product page (https://www.h3c.com/en/Products_and_Solutions/InterConnect/Switches/Products/Campus_Network/Access/S5130/H3C_S5130S_EI/). Current software line is Comware 7 CMW710, release R6381 listed on the H3C resource centre for this series (https://www.h3c.com/en/Support/Resource_Center/EN/Switches/Catalog/S5130S/S5130S-EI/default.htm). Two fans, 440 x 320 x 43.6 mm, <= 4.5 kg, 24.5 W minimum / 420 W maximum draw (PoE 370 W), 80 Gbps maximum stacking bandwidth, serial console only. The vendor port table prints the uplinks as 2*10G SFP+ plus 2*1/2.5/5/10G BASE-T, i.e. a copper multigig pair beside the two cages; they are modelled here on the Ten-GigabitEthernet numbering with the copper pair negotiating 1G/2.5G/5G/10G."
